      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Currently, there is no single global industry standard because platforms like x, Facebook, and TikTok establish their own distinct guidelines based on their specific risk tolerance and regional regulations. Most major platforms generally exempt political satire only when it clearly targets a protected group and contains incitement, while flagging unambiguous hate speech regardless of satirical intent. Given the ambiguity of your new platform, you should likely adopt a precedent like x's approach, which distinguishes hyperbolic views from targeted harassment, though consulting legal counsel for your specific jurisdiction is crucial before finalizing these rules.",
